.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-LIST-ROLES 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-list-roles \- list the roles this account can bind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eam list-roles
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-x\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fIFIELD\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-direction\fR|\fB\-r\fR \fIasc\fR|\fIdesc\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-builtin\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists every role a grant in your account can name: the seven built-in ones,
then your account's own.
.SH THE SEVEN BUILT-IN ROLES
.TP
.B account-administrator
Everything, within the account a grant of it names. That is
.IR *:* ,
which does not reach
.I emm
or
.I emd
\- so it is the strongest thing a role can say and still not
installation administration.
.TP
.B operator
Every action except the destructive ones and access management.
.TP
.B reader
Every action that only reads.
.TP
.B publisher
Send to a queue, publish to a topic, and resolve the two by name.
.TP
.B consumer
Take messages off a queue and manage a topic subscription.
.TP
.B application
What a euclid-deployed application is given: publish, consume, read and
write objects, and own the delivery queue it consumes through \- create
it, list it, subscribe it to a topic or a bucket, and delete it again.
An application receives from a queue of its own rather than from the
topic directly, so that queue is part of the application. It still
cannot delete the topic or the bucket it subscribes to. Always granted
with an explicit resource list.
.TP
.B transfer
Everything an FTP or SFTP client can do on a transfer server: list,
download, upload, rename, and create and remove directories \- plus the
four ESM object actions those turn into, since a transfer server keeps
nothing of its own and reaches the bucket as the client. The one
built-in that spans two modules, and the one that names a short list
rather than following a rule. See
.BR euclid-cli-ets (1).
.PP
There is deliberately no
.I administrator
role. Installation administration is membership of the
.I administrator
user group, not a grant \- roles are per account and an installation
administrator is by definition not, and
.I emm
has to be reachable by something when no
.I emm
permission exists to grant. See
.B ADMINISTRATOR PRIVILEGES
in
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1).
.SH WHY THEY ARE NOT PAGED
The built-in roles come first and ignore
.B \-\-page\-size
and
.BR \-\-page\-index .
They are computed rather than stored, so there is no page to put them on
\-
.I reader
is "every action that reads" applied to the permission vocabulary on this
build, not a row somebody wrote. A module that gains a
.I list\-widgets
action gains it in
.I reader
and
.I operator
at the same time, in every account, with nobody to remember.
.PP
For the same reason,
.B total
counts your account's own roles only. Use
.B \-\-no\-builtin
for a listing where paging and the count describe the same set.
.PP
.B \-\-prefix
does apply to both.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only roles whose name starts with this. Defaults to empty, which is all
of them.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of stored roles to return. Defaults to \fI10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index. Defaults to \fI0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fIFIELD\fR
Field to sort the stored roles by. Defaults to \fIname\fR.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-sort\-direction " " \fIasc\fR|\fIdesc\fR
Sort direction. Defaults to \fIasc\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-builtin
Leave out the built-in roles.
.SH WHO MAY RUN IT
Installation administrators \- members of the
.I administrator
user group. See
.B ADMINISTRATOR PRIVILEGES
in
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The roles were listed.
.TP
.B 1
The request could not be sent, or the caller is not an administrator. If
the failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the
stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# What this account can bind, built-ins included
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-roles

# Only the roles this account wrote itself
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-roles --no-builtin

# The service roles, newest page size
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-roles \e
    --prefix svc- --page-size 50
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-get-role (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-role (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-update-role (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-role (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-role (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-permissions (1)
